cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  LC-Intention-NAS: hardware-constrained neural architecture search for
  lane-change intention and time-to-lane-change prediction
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sepehr
    family-names: Mohammady
    affiliation: >-
      ELIOS Lab, Department of Electrical, Electronic and Telecommunications
      Engineering and Naval Architecture (DITEN), University of Genoa, Italy
repository-code: https://github.com/SepehrMohammady/LC-Intention-NAS
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Constrained neural architecture search for driver-intention and
  surrounding-vehicle manoeuvre prediction, evaluated on two driving datasets
  and deployed to Arm Cortex-M microcontrollers with measured flash, RAM and
  inference latency from the ST Edge AI board farm.
keywords:
  - neural architecture search
  - TinyML
  - lane change prediction
  - time to lane change
  - quantization
  - STM32
  - embedded machine learning
  - intelligent transportation systems
references:
